INT. ABANDONED PLANETARIUM - NIGHT

The dome is cracked, the stars on it long gone to water stains. A circle of folding chairs sits beneath the central projector, a bulbous metal insect. Candle stubs flicker on the floor.

Four people sit in the circle, coats on, breath fogging.

MAGDALENA "MAGGIE" OYELOWO-SZABO is in her fifties, wrapped in a quilt, a retired astronomer's patience in her eyes. Across from her, her adult son DAMIAN KELLERMAN-ASANTE slouches, jaw tight. Beside him sits his wife YOLANDE BEAUMONT-DAS, tall, steady, hand on his knee. The fourth chair holds ELIJAH "ELI" ROSENBLATT-ADEBAYO, a teenager in a hooded jacket, cradling a battered telescope case.

MAGGIE
Thank you for coming, all of you.

DAMIAN
Mom, why are we here?

MAGGIE
Because the city is closing this building on Friday.

DAMIAN
And?

MAGGIE
And I wanted to show you the sky one more time.

YOLANDE
Maggie, the projector's dead.

MAGGIE
Is it?

She stands. Crosses to the great machine. Lays her palm on its flank, the way you'd greet an old horse. She reaches into a panel, draws out a bulb the size of a fist, and screws it home.

Eli slides forward in his seat.

ELI
You fixed it?

MAGGIE
I did, Eli. Last Tuesday.

DAMIAN
You came here every night this week.

MAGGIE
Every night.

DAMIAN
Without telling anyone.

MAGGIE
Without telling anyone, Damian.

Silence. Yolande squeezes her husband's knee. He looks at the floor.

YOLANDE
Damian. Let her.

Maggie throws a switch. The machine whirs, coughs dust, and then blooms. On the dome, thousands of pinpoints appear, slow, shuddering, then steady. The Milky Way rolls out across the ceiling like a shaken scarf.

Eli gasps. Yolande puts her hand to her mouth. Damian lifts his head, and the light spills across his face.

DAMIAN
(hoarse)
That's the one from the lake house.

MAGGIE
That's the one.

DAMIAN
You said you couldn't make it that clear again.

MAGGIE
I said a lot of things after your father died.

Damian rises. Walks across the circle. Stands in front of her. He doesn't speak. She waits. Then, awkwardly, like a man unused to it, he wraps his arms around her.

MAGGIE (CONT'D)
(into his shoulder)
There now.

ELI
Can I look through the scope?

MAGGIE
Oh, Eli. There's no sky left to look through. But sit. Sit. There's plenty of dome.
